WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.240
This house, located in the beautiful&nbsp;
mountain village of Asago, Japan, is free.

00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:10.500
Not “free-to-the-one-millionth-visitor free”.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:17.280
Not free except for these terms&nbsp;
and conditions free. Just… free.

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:20.820
Some of the top amenities include:

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:27.360
These ruins of a 15th-century castle,&nbsp;
a mere 20-minute scenic drive away.

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:33.360
And everything from Cherry Blossom&nbsp;
trees, to a supermarket, post office,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:36.840
and hair salon — all within walking distance.

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:44.880
Now, the building itself is no five-star hotel,&nbsp;
it could use more than a fresh coat of paint.

00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:51.060
But at nearly 1,400 square feet,&nbsp;
with two stories, flush toilets,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:55.080
and heating, there are worse&nbsp;
ways to spend zero dollars.

00:00:56.460 --> 00:01:01.440
More remarkable, perhaps, is the fact&nbsp;
that this deal isn’t all that remarkable.

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:08.520
There are at least eight million such&nbsp;
abandoned homes across Japan — some free&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:13.500
and others effectively free — just&nbsp;
waiting for someone to claim them.

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:17.880
Maybe the island lifestyle is more your speed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:22.860
in which case you might be interested in&nbsp;
this one for about $5,000 U.S. dollars.

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:28.440
If you’re looking to splurge a bit, this&nbsp;
one could be yours for eleven grand.

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:31.320
The possibilities are endless.

00:01:32.580 --> 00:01:36.540
You can have your pick between&nbsp;
about one in every seven houses,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.540 --> 00:01:43.260
including the land, 11% of the entire&nbsp;
country’s surface area — and there’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:47.640
no hurry — these numbers are&nbsp;
expected to double by 2033.

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:54.300
That’s right, in just ten years’ time, nearly&nbsp;
every third Japanese home will be vacant,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:58.080
according to the country’s largest&nbsp;
economic research institute.

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:03.000
And while its population is among&nbsp;
the fastest shrinking in the world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:08.160
demography alone cannot explain&nbsp;
these strange real estate dynamics.

